NEWFS(8)	    UNIX Programmer's Manual		 NEWFS(8)



	  NNOOTTEE:: Mkfs deals in units of filesystem blocks not sec-
	  tors.  Newfs uses sectors.

FFIILLEESS
     /etc/disktab   disk geometry and partition information
     mkfs to actually build the file system

SSEEEE AALLSSOO
     getdisklabel(3), disklabel(8), disktab(5), diskpart(8),
     fs(5), fsck(8), mkfs(8)

BBUUGGSS
     nneewwffss(8) no longer places boot blocks on the filesystem.
     That duty has been moved to the ddiisskkllaabbeell(8) program.  If
     you must place a boot block on a disk whose driver does not
     support disklabels use dddd(1).







































